  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Local Capacity for Economic Development in Aymara Municipalities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SEMTA will undertake a program of agricultural development benefiting 400 Aymara families from 34 communities in three municipalities in Pacajes. It expects to increase harvests of quinoa, canawi and vegetables; the production of camelids, cattle and sheep; and native and exotic pastures. The introduction of related technologies should improve access to water for livestock, agriculture and human consumption, and reverse environmental degradation. (BO-523)</narrative>
  </description>
